      \field{abstract}{This paper focuses on the impacts of climate physical risks on crop prices and proposes a novel method to evaluate the vulnerability of five agricultural commodities, i.e., wheat, maize, soybean, rice, and barley. We identified the high vulnerability of maize and high resistance of rice to shocks of physical risks. During the period from 2020 to 2022, the vulnerability of global agricultural commodity markets sharply rose. The findings provide novel insight into the influence of climate change on agricultural sectors.}
